This file applies to the original code in this repository: the sources, scripts, tests and documents
that carry "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT". Copyright (c) 2026 Anurodh Pokharel. Each file's SPDX line
is authoritative for that file. The full text is also in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

History: the code was GPL-2.0-only while the browser linked the earlier engine (GPL-2.0-only) and had files
derived from its frontends. None of that is on this branch (the earlier UI lives at the tag `legacy-engine` and keeps its GPL
terms there), so the original code here is relicensed by its copyright holder.

Exceptions, which keep their own terms:
  frontend/assets/icons/        the Lucide icons (ISC; chevrons, x, plus and lock also MIT via Feather):
                                see frontend/assets/icons/LICENSE-lucide.txt, which must travel with them
  compat/include/libproc.h,     small interface declarations (struct layouts, constants, prototypes) modelled on
  compat/include/sys/           Apple's XNU / macOS headers: APSL-2.0 (LICENSES/APSL-2.0.txt), as their SPDX lines say
    proc_info.h, random.h
  tools/bind_audit.sh           vendored from the xnu-iokit-pi3 port; its licence is that repo's
  scripts/webkit_fixes.sh       the file is MIT, but the edits it applies to the WebKit tree (and the one
                                small source file it writes into it) become part of WebKit and are under
                                WebKit's licences (LGPL-2 and BSD-2-Clause)

Third-party sources that setup_third_party.sh fetches (WebKit, GLib, ICU, LLVM's libc++, libsoup, OpenSSL,
libjpeg-turbo, the CA bundle and the other libraries) keep their own licences; Florence links the
LGPL ones as shared libraries and does not copy them into this repository.
